// ---- BEES TEMPUS node (T3): pasted by tools/bees_tempus_gen.py (--part bees_tempus_node.part) into the dangerous_ root
// unit of a program that is a TEMPUS node, after the TEMPUS link edge (bees_tempus_link.part). The node actor is here
// because it dials (the carrier's spawn site stays in the root unit, SD-17). development-plan/tempus-design.md sections
// 3 to 6, 8 to 10 and 16.3. Nothing here reads a file or holds a default: every value is an argument.
//
// tempus_node_start(app, idn, net, sz, drv) -> the node actor. It listens, joins through its sentinels, serves admitted
// peers and ticks its three stores.
//   app   the application's actor; it is told (:bees, op, s1, "", 0, 0, node): 80 the node's own token is not valid any
//         more and ticking has stopped (s1: why); 81 a peer answered key_rotated (s1: the kid it named); 86 the system
//         clock could not be read (s1: what that means for the node; told once per failure, not once per reading);
//         87 the system clock went back by more than clock_back_limit_s under clock_back stop and the node has stopped
//         (s1: the line): it does not tick, closes every accepted connection at once, and stays so whatever is read
//         later, until the application starts a node again
//   idn   { id, pub, seed, addr, token, typ }: the TEMPUS identity (peer id, public key, private seed), the address other
//         nodes dial, the producer's token, the node's own type (1 edge, 2 bridge, 3 sentinel)
//   net   { listen, spec, sents, wl, kid, ppub, ms, mst, max, skew, j0, j1, back, blim, fail, every }: the carrier's listen text; the engine's
//         credential text (tempus_spec); the sentinels as "a.b.c.d:port,..." ("" for a first sentinel); the tempus
//         whitelist (128 hex characters per certificate); the current producer key; shuffle_timeout_ms as a number and
//         as text; inflight_max; clock_skew in seconds; join_retry_initial_ms and join_retry_max_ms; clock_back (what a
//         reading earlier than the node's time does: 1 follow, 2 hold, 3 stop); clock_back_limit_s (under stop, the
//         greatest step back in seconds still followed; not read under follow and hold); clock_fail (what a reading
//         that fails after a good one does: 1 continue, 2 pause); clock_read_ms (how often the system clock is read).
//         None of the four has a default: tempus_node_boot refuses a choice outside its set. An externally driven
//         node is given its readings by its driver and judges each by the same choices; clock_read_ms is not used by it.
//   sz    { k1, c1, t1, k2, c2, t2, k3, c3, t3 }: capacity, shuffle length and tick_ms of the edge, bridge and sentinel store
//   drv   { driven, ext, draws }: a production application passes { driven: false, ext: its own actor, draws: "" }:
//         ext and draws are then never read. driven true makes the node EXTERNALLY DRIVEN (design 16.3; owner's ruling
//         of 2026-11-20): it starts no clock actor and no store timers and waits for the messages those would send,
//         from whoever holds its actor reference; its draws are the literal list `draws` ("3,0,7") and it prints one
//         line per view change; and a well-formed frame of no tempus/1 kind from an admitted peer is handed to the
//         actor `ext` (below). Nothing drives such a node by itself: until somebody casts it a first clock reading it
//         does not listen, join or tick. tempus_node_boot refuses driven on a listen address that is not loopback.
//         THIS FILE HOLDS NO TEST FRAME: nothing here, and nothing in src/tempus, decodes or answers a tick or a clock
//         frame, with or without `driven`. The unit that does is src/tempus_test/bees_tempus_test.silica, which only a
//         test program lists in its build and passes as `ext`.
// What a driver casts to an externally driven node (the node's own clock actor and timers send the first two forms
// with n or m 0 and get no answer):
//   (:bees, 130, "", "", seconds or -1, tag, who)   a clock reading, judged like the system clock's (tn_clock). With a
//         tag other than 0 on a driven node, `ext` is told (:bees, 132, "", "", tag, 0, who) when the reading is taken
//   (:bees, 1, "", "", tag, store, who)             one tick of that store. With a tag other than 0 on a driven node,
//         `ext` is told (:bees, 131, "", "", tag, 0, who) when the tick has ended: when the shuffle it started has
//         ended (merged, failed or timed out), or at once when it started none
// What `ext` is told by a driven node, besides 131 and 132: once, at the node's start, (:bees, 133, the listen text, "",
// 0, 0, the node), so that it knows the node it drives; and (:bees, 68, body, the peer's descriptor, cid, m, conn),
// an admitted peer's frame of no tempus/1 kind, as 63 below; it must answer `conn` exactly once: (:bees, 20, reply
// body, "", 0), or (:bees, 21, "", "", 0) to close with no reply, or (:bees, 22, why, "", 0) to have the connection
// actor refuse the frame as it does on a node that is not driven (audit line protocol_error, a bridge scores it).
// What the application may cast to the node, as (:bees, op, s1, s2, 0, 0, app):
//   70 a new token (s1)       71 a new producer key (s1: kid, s2: the 32-byte key; ruling NQ-5)
//
// The clock (ruling NQ-11). An externally driven node's clock is the readings its driver casts. Any other node reads the
// system clock through the TEMPUS native edge (bees_tempus_wall_clock: whole seconds since 1970; an error of the
// operating system is refused, never replaced by a made-up time). The reading is asked for by the node's clock actor
// (dangerous_bees_tempus_draws@tck) at start and once a second after each answer, and the node's clock is the last
// reading. Such a node does not listen, join or tick before its first reading: with no clock it can check no token.
// What a later reading that fails does, and what a reading EARLIER than the node's time does, are the application's
// choices clock_fail and clock_back (ruling NQ-22 of 2026-11-20; design section 10). The whole decision is the pure
// bees_tempus_node@clock_turn; tn_clock prints its lines and does what it says.
// An externally driven node's stores are ticked by its driver's messages only; otherwise each store has its own timer.
// One bound for a connection (ruling NQ-14): shuffle_timeout_ms from the dial, or the accept, to the close; the link
// part turns it into one deadline that the connect budget, the handshake and the admitted connection share.
//
// What the node waits for is one list of { k, cid, st, x, who }:
//   k 1 a partner's shuffle and k 2 a sample, each waiting for store st (cid: the accepted connection, who: its actor)
//   k 3 a tick of store st whose first answer has not come (cid 0: the timer's; else a driver's tag, who: the actor
//       reference the driver gave with it, handed back in 131)
//   k 4 a tick of store st whose shuffle is in flight
//   k 5 the dialed connection cid of store st's shuffle     k 6 the dialed connection cid of a sample to sentinel x / 2
//       (x odd: part of the join at start, which goes on to the next store and retries; x even: asked again after a
//       tick found the view empty)                          k 7 that sample's entries on their way into the store
//       (s: the descriptor of the sentinel that answered, when it is one: ruling NQ-12)
//   k 9 that sentinel's own entry on its way into the node's sentinel store (ruling NQ-12: a joiner keeps the sentinel
//       it joined through), after the sample's entries are in
//   k 2 with x 1: a sentinel's insert of the asking peer is still on its way; k 8: the sample is ready (s: the reply
//       body, x: 1 ok) and waits for that insert, so the node's lines about one connection come before its reply
fn tn_say(s: string) -> atom {
    sequence proc[device_io]
        _: atom <- println(s)
    produces pure :ok end
}
fn tn_num(n: int64) -> string { bees_trust_frame@int_text(n) }
fn tn_typ(t: int64) -> string { bees_tempus_node@typ_text(t) }
fn tn_null() -> actor_ref { actor_ref_of_word(0) }
// the node's clock: the last reading it was given (tn_clock): the system clock's, or its driver's (ruling NQ-11)
fn tn_now(c: $NC$, v: $NV$) -> int64 { v.now }
fn tn_count(c: $NC$, st: int64) -> int64 { case st of { 1 -> c.c1; 2 -> c.c2; _: int64 -> c.c3 } }
fn tn_maxcount(c: $NC$) -> int64 {
    m: int64 <- case c.c1 > c.c2 of { true -> c.c1; false -> c.c2 };
    case m > c.c3 of { true -> m; false -> c.c3 }
}
fn tn_adp(v: $NV$, st: int64) -> actor_ref { case st of { 1 -> v.a1; 2 -> v.a2; _: int64 -> v.a3 } }
fn tn_desc(c: $NC$, v: $NV$) -> $D$ { bees_tempus_frame@desc(c.id, c.pub, c.addr, v.mtok) }
fn tn_cfg(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, count: int64) -> $CFG$ {
    mine: string <- bees_tempus_frame@enc_advert(tn_desc(c, v));
    { node: me, sig: c.sig, edge: c.edge, rnd: c.rnd, mine: mine, mtok: v.mtok, kid: v.kid, ppub: v.ppub, wl: c.wl, now: tn_now(c, v), skew: c.skew, count: count, ms: c.ms, ext: c.driven }
}
fn tn_to(v: $NV$, st: int64, op: int64, id: string, d: string, n: int64) -> boolean {
    bees_tempus_node@to_adp(tn_adp(v, st), op, id, d, n)
}
// the answer to an accepted connection: 20 a reply body, 21 close with no reply
fn tn_ans(who: actor_ref, k: int64, body: string) -> boolean {
    sequence proc[concurrency]
        ok: boolean <- cast(who, (:bees, k, body, "", 0) impl ActorMessage {})
    produces pure ok end
}
fn tn_app(c: $NC$, me: actor_ref, op: int64, s1: string) -> boolean {
    sequence proc[concurrency]
        ok: boolean <- cast(c.app, (:bees, op, s1, "", 0, 0, me) impl ActorMessage {})
    produces pure ok end
}
fn tn_vq(v: $NV$, q: $PL$) -> $NV$ {
    { up: v.up, rc: v.rc, a1: v.a1, a2: v.a2, a3: v.a3, now: v.now, ck: v.ck, mtok: v.mtok, kid: v.kid, ppub: v.ppub, live: v.live, na: v.na, nd: v.nd, stop: v.stop, jst: v.jst, jd: v.jd, q: q }
}
fn tn_vc(v: $NV$, live: int64, na: int64, nd: int64) -> $NV$ {
    { up: v.up, rc: v.rc, a1: v.a1, a2: v.a2, a3: v.a3, now: v.now, ck: v.ck, mtok: v.mtok, kid: v.kid, ppub: v.ppub, live: live, na: na, nd: nd, stop: v.stop, jst: v.jst, jd: v.jd, q: v.q }
}
fn tn_vj(v: $NV$, jst: int64, jd: uint64) -> $NV$ {
    { up: v.up, rc: v.rc, a1: v.a1, a2: v.a2, a3: v.a3, now: v.now, ck: v.ck, mtok: v.mtok, kid: v.kid, ppub: v.ppub, live: v.live, na: v.na, nd: v.nd, stop: v.stop, jst: jst, jd: jd, q: v.q }
}
fn tn_vclk(v: $NV$, now: int64, ck: int64) -> $NV$ {
    { up: v.up, rc: v.rc, a1: v.a1, a2: v.a2, a3: v.a3, now: now, ck: ck, mtok: v.mtok, kid: v.kid, ppub: v.ppub, live: v.live, na: v.na, nd: v.nd, stop: v.stop, jst: v.jst, jd: v.jd, q: v.q }
}
fn tn_vk(v: $NV$, now: int64, mtok: string, kid: string, ppub: string, stop: boolean) -> $NV$ {
    { up: v.up, rc: v.rc, a1: v.a1, a2: v.a2, a3: v.a3, now: now, ck: v.ck, mtok: mtok, kid: kid, ppub: ppub, live: v.live, na: v.na, nd: v.nd, stop: stop, jst: v.jst, jd: v.jd, q: v.q }
}
fn tn_wait(v: $NV$, k: int64, cid: int64, st: int64, who: actor_ref) -> $NV$ {
    p: $P$ <- { k: k, cid: cid, st: st, x: 0, who: who, s: "" };
    tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_push(v.q, p))
}
// one audit line of the node about an accepted connection's request, in the form of the connection's own lines
fn tn_audit(r: $RQ$, event: string, what: string) -> atom {
    pd: { ok: boolean, d: $D$ } <- bees_tempus_frame@desc_of(r.pd);
    d: $D$ <- pd.d;
    tn_say(concat(concat(concat("[tempus audit] ", event), concat(" peer=", bees_trust_frame@cut(bees_trust_frame@hex(d.id), 0, 16))), concat(concat(" ", what), concat(" a", tn_num(r.cid)))))
}
fn tn_refuse(v: $NV$, r: $RQ$, event: string, what: string) -> $NV$ {
    sequence
        _: atom <- tn_audit(r, event, what);
        _: boolean <- tn_ans(r.who, 21, "")
    produces pure v end
}

// ---- the join (section 6): one sample per store to a sentinel
fn tn_dbl(jd: uint64, j1: uint64) -> uint64 {
    n: uint64 <- jd * 2;
    case n > j1 of { true -> j1; false -> n }
}
// Ruling NQ-22 (1.d, 2026-11-20): while the node waits for its clock after a failed reading (v.ck 2, clock_fail pause) it
// dials nobody, so a join's dial (a retry timer, or the next store after an answer) is remembered and not made: v.jst is
// 10 + the store. tn_clock makes it at once when the clock is read again. After a stop (v.ck 4) nothing is dialed.
fn tn_join(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, st: int64, x: int64) -> $NV$ {
    case v.ck == 2 of {
        true -> { sequence _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat("join: the request for ", tn_typ(st)), " waits until the system clock is read again")) produces pure tn_vj(v, 10 + st, v.jd) end };
        false -> case v.ck == 4 of { true -> v; false -> tn_join_dial(c, v, me, st, x) }
    }
}
fn tn_join_dial(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, st: int64, x: int64) -> $NV$ {
    cid: int64 <- v.nd + 1;
    addr: string <- bees_tempus_node@csv_nth(c.sents, x / 2);
    cfg: $CFG$ <- tn_cfg(c, v, me, tn_count(c, st));
    p: $P$ <- { k: 6, cid: cid, st: st, x: x, who: tn_null(), s: "" };
    sequence
        _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat(concat("join: asking the sentinel at ", addr), concat(" for ", tn_typ(st))), concat(" d", tn_num(cid))));
        _: boolean <- tempus_dial(cfg, addr, bees_tempus_frame@enc_sample(st, tn_count(c, st)), cid, c.spec, c.mst, c.ms);
        v1: $NV$ <- tn_vc(v, v.live, v.na, cid)
    produces pure tn_vq(v1, bees_tempus_node@p_push(v.q, p)) end
}
fn tn_join_start(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref) -> $NV$ {
    case bees_tempus_node@csv_count(c.sents) == 0 of {
        true -> { sequence _: atom <- tn_say("join: no sentinel is configured") produces pure tn_vj(v, 4, c.j0) end };
        false -> tn_join(c, tn_vj(v, 1, c.j0), me, 1, 1)
    }
}
fn tn_join_ok(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, p: $P$) -> $NV$ {
    case p.x % 2 == 1 of {
        false -> v;
        true -> case p.st < 3 of {
            true -> tn_join(c, tn_vj(v, p.st + 1, c.j0), me, p.st + 1, 1);
            false -> { sequence _: atom <- tn_say("join: done") produces pure tn_vj(v, 4, c.j0) end }
        }
    }
}
fn tn_join_failed(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, p: $P$) -> $NV$ {
    case p.x / 2 + 1 < bees_tempus_node@csv_count(c.sents) of {
        true -> tn_join(c, v, me, p.st, p.x + 2);
        false -> case p.x % 2 == 1 of {
            false -> { sequence _: atom <- tn_say(concat("join: no sentinel answered for ", tn_typ(p.st))) produces pure v end };
            true -> {
                sequence proc[concurrency]
                    _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat("join: no sentinel answered for ", tn_typ(p.st)), "; waiting to try again"));
                    t: timer_ref <- send_after(v.jd, me, (:bees, 72, "", "", p.st, 0, me) impl ActorMessage {})
                produces pure tn_vj(v, p.st, tn_dbl(v.jd, c.j1)) end
            }
        }
    }
}

// ---- ticks
fn tn_own_why(c: $NC$, v: $NV$) -> string {
    p: { why: string, payload: string, sig: string } <- bees_tempus_admit@pre(tn_desc(c, v), v.kid, tn_now(c, v), c.skew, 0);
    p.why
}
// a tick has ended. The timer's tick (tag 0) tells nobody. A driver's tick (tag other than 0; an externally driven node
// only) is told to the node's extension actor, with the actor reference the driver gave: (:bees, 131, "", "", tag, 0, who)
fn tn_done(c: $NC$, cid: int64, who: actor_ref) -> boolean {
    case cid != 0 and c.driven of {
        false -> true;
        true -> {
            sequence proc[concurrency]
                ok: boolean <- cast(c.ext, (:bees, 131, "", "", cid, 0, who) impl ActorMessage {})
            produces pure ok end
        }
    }
}
fn tn_tick(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, st: int64, p: $P$) -> $NV$ {
    why: string <- tn_own_why(c, v);
    case length_bytes(why) > 0 of {
        true -> {
            sequence
                _: atom <- case v.stop of { true -> :ok; false -> tn_say(concat(concat("own token: ", why), "; ticking has stopped")) };
                _: boolean <- case v.stop of { true -> true; false -> tn_app(c, me, 80, why) };
                _: boolean <- tn_done(c, p.cid, p.who)
            produces pure tn_vk(v, v.now, v.mtok, v.kid, v.ppub, true) end
        };
        false -> {
            sequence
                _: boolean <- tn_to(v, st, 46, "", "", tn_now(c, v))
            produces pure tn_wait(v, 3, p.cid, st, p.who) end
        }
    }
}
fn tn_how(n: int64) -> string {
    case n of { 0 -> "aged only (a shuffle is in flight)"; 1 -> "shuffle merged"; 2 -> "shuffle failed"; 3 -> "skipped (no draws)"; _: int64 -> "the view is empty" }
}
// the store's shuffle goes out (120)
fn tn_out(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, st: int64, pdesc: string, body: string) -> $NV$ {
    w: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_first(v.q, 3, st);
    v1: $NV$ <- tn_wait(tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_drop(v.q, w)), 4, w.cid, st, w.who);
    pd: { ok: boolean, d: $D$ } <- bees_tempus_frame@desc_of(pdesc);
    d: $D$ <- pd.d;
    cid: int64 <- v.nd + 1;
    head: string <- concat(concat(concat("tick ", tn_typ(st)), ": shuffle with "), bees_tempus_node@peer8(d.id));
    case bees_tempus_node@addr_ok(d.addr) of {
        false -> {
            sequence
                _: atom <- tn_say(concat(head, ": its address is not one this build dials"));
                _: boolean <- tn_to(v, st, 42, "", "", 0)
            produces pure v1 end
        };
        true -> {
            cfg: $CFG$ <- tn_cfg(c, v, me, tn_count(c, st));
            sequence
                _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat(concat(head, " at "), d.addr), concat(" d", tn_num(cid))));
                _: boolean <- tempus_dial(cfg, d.addr, body, cid, c.spec, c.mst, c.ms);
                v2: $NV$ <- tn_wait(v1, 5, cid, st, tn_null())
            produces pure tn_vc(v2, v2.live, v2.na, cid) end
        }
    }
}
// a tick has ended (124)
fn tn_ended(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, st: int64, how: int64) -> $NV$ {
    w: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_first(v.q, case how == 1 or how == 2 of { true -> 4; false -> 3 }, st);
    v1: $NV$ <- tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_drop(v.q, w));
    j6: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_first(v.q, 6, st);
    j7: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_first(v.q, 7, st);
    j: $P$ <- case j6.k == 0 of { true -> j7; false -> j6 };
    again: boolean <- how == 4 and v.jst == 4 and j.k == 0 and bees_tempus_node@csv_count(c.sents) > 0;
    sequence
        _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat(concat("tick ", tn_typ(st)), ": "), tn_how(how)));
        _: boolean <- tn_done(c, w.cid, w.who);
        v2: $NV$ <- case again of { true -> tn_join(c, v1, me, st, 0); false -> v1 }
    produces pure v2 end
}

// ---- a dialed connection's outcome (60 a reply, 61 failed, 62 key_rotated)
fn tn_dialed_shuffle(v: $NV$, p: $P$, op: int64, s1: string, what: string) -> $NV$ {
    case op == 60 of {
        true -> { sequence _: boolean <- tn_to(v, p.st, 41, "", s1, 0) produces pure v end };
        false -> {
            sequence
                _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat(concat("tick ", tn_typ(p.st)), concat(": the partner did not answer, ", what)), concat(" d", tn_num(p.cid))));
                _: boolean <- tn_to(v, p.st, 42, "", "", 0)
            produces pure v end
        }
    }
}
// sd: the descriptor of the peer that answered when its token says tempus_sentinel (its certificate is then one of the
// whitelist: the connection actor's rule), else "": it goes into the node's sentinel store after the sample's entries
fn tn_dialed_join(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, p: $P$, s1: string, what: string, sd: string) -> $NV$ {
    case bees_tempus_frame@kind(s1) == 8 of {
        true -> {
            sequence
                _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat("join: the sentinel answered for ", tn_typ(p.st)), concat(" d", tn_num(p.cid))));
                _: boolean <- tn_to(v, p.st, 43, "", s1, 0 - p.cid);
                w: $P$ <- { k: 7, cid: p.cid, st: p.st, x: p.x, who: p.who, s: sd }
            produces pure tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_push(v.q, w)) end
        };
        false -> {
            sequence
                _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat(concat("join: the sentinel did not answer for ", tn_typ(p.st)), concat(", ", what)), concat(" d", tn_num(p.cid))));
                v2: $NV$ <- tn_join_failed(c, v, me, p)
            produces pure v2 end
        }
    }
}
fn tn_dialed(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, op: int64, s1: string, cid: int64, pd: string, m: int64) -> $NV$ {
    p: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_cid(v.q, cid, 5, 6);
    v1: $NV$ <- tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_drop(v.q, p));
    what: string <- case op == 62 of { true -> "key_rotated"; false -> s1 };
    sequence
        _: boolean <- case op == 62 of { true -> tn_app(c, me, 81, s1); false -> true };
        v2: $NV$ <- case p.k of {
            5 -> tn_dialed_shuffle(v1, p, op, s1, what);
            6 -> tn_dialed_join(c, v1, me, p, case op == 60 of { true -> s1; false -> "" }, what, case op == 60 and m % 4 == 3 of { true -> pd; false -> "" });
            _: int64 -> v
        }
    produces pure v2 end
}

// ---- an admitted peer's request (63)
fn tn_rq_shuffle(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, r: $RQ$) -> $NV$ {
    e: { ok: boolean, why: string, store: int64, entries: $L$ } <- bees_tempus_frame@dec_entries(r.body, tn_maxcount(c));
    pd: { ok: boolean, d: $D$ } <- bees_tempus_frame@desc_of(r.pd);
    d: $D$ <- pd.d;
    case e.ok of {
        false -> tn_refuse(v, r, "protocol_error", e.why);
        true -> {
            sequence
                _: boolean <- tn_to(v, e.store, 40, d.id, r.body, r.cid)
            produces pure tn_wait(v, 1, r.cid, e.store, r.who) end
        }
    }
}
fn tn_rq_sample(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, r: $RQ$) -> $NV$ {
    s0: { ok: boolean, why: string, store: int64, n: int64 } <- bees_tempus_frame@dec_sample(r.body, bees_tempus_frame@entries_max());
    s: { ok: boolean, why: string, store: int64, n: int64 } <- bees_tempus_frame@dec_sample(r.body, tn_count(c, s0.store));
    pd: { ok: boolean, d: $D$ } <- bees_tempus_frame@desc_of(r.pd);
    d: $D$ <- pd.d;
    case s0.ok and s.ok of {
        false -> tn_refuse(v, r, "protocol_error", case s0.ok of { true -> s.why; false -> s0.why });
        true -> {
            sequence
                _: boolean <- tn_to(v, s.store, 45, "", "", s.n);
                // a sentinel inserts the peer that asks it into its store of the peer's type (the join, section 6), after
                // the sample was taken; the answer goes out when both are done (x 1: the insert is still on its way)
                _: boolean <- case c.typ == 3 of { true -> tn_to(v, r.m % 4, 44, d.id, r.pd, r.cid); false -> true };
                w: $P$ <- { k: 2, cid: r.cid, st: s.store, x: case c.typ == 3 of { true -> 1; false -> 0 }, who: r.who, s: "" }
            produces pure tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_push(v.q, w)) end
        }
    }
}
fn tn_request(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, r: $RQ$) -> $NV$ {
    k: int64 <- bees_tempus_frame@kind(r.body);
    case k of {
        5 -> tn_rq_shuffle(c, v, r);
        7 -> tn_rq_sample(c, v, r);
        12 -> tn_rq_call(c, v, r);
        13 -> tn_rq_call(c, v, r);
        _: int64 -> tn_refuse(v, r, "request_refused", "call and cast are served by a bridge only")
    }
}
// A frame of no tempus/1 kind (68). The connection actor sends it on an externally driven node only (cfg.ext), after its
// structure check; a node that is not driven refuses it here as well, so nothing depends on that one check. The driven
// node hands it to its extension actor unread, which answers the connection actor itself, exactly once.
fn tn_rq_ext(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, b: $NB$) -> $NV$ {
    r: $RQ$ <- { body: b.s1, pd: b.s2, cid: b.n, m: b.m, who: b.who };
    case c.driven of {
        false -> tn_refuse(v, r, "protocol_error", "not a request: unknown kind");
        true -> {
            sequence proc[concurrency]
                ok: boolean <- cast(c.ext, (:bees, 68, b.s1, b.s2, b.n, b.m, b.who) impl ActorMessage {})
            produces pure v end
        }
    }
}
// T6: on a bridge (role 2) a call or cast goes to the node's application, which on a bridge is the table actor of
// src/tempus/bees_tempus_bridge.silica (tbr): it answers the connection actor itself, exactly once. m carries the node's
// clock (seconds * 65536) beside the connection's whitelist index and peer type (m < 65536). Any other node refuses.
fn tn_rq_call(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, r: $RQ$) -> $NV$ {
    case c.typ == 2 of {
        false -> tn_refuse(v, r, "request_refused", "call and cast are served by a bridge only");
        true -> {
            sequence proc[concurrency]
                ok: boolean <- cast(c.app, (:bees, 82, r.body, r.pd, r.cid, tn_now(c, v) * 65536 + r.m, r.who) impl ActorMessage {})
            produces pure v end
        }
    }
}
// Ruling NQ-19: the connection actor refused an accepted peer (67; s1 the audit event; m 1: s2 the peer's descriptor,
// verified; m 0: s2 the peer's id alone). On a bridge the table actor is told (83) with the node's clock, as with 82,
// and raises that peer's score; any other node keeps no score and drops it.
fn tn_refused_peer(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, b: $NB$) -> $NV$ {
    case c.typ == 2 of {
        false -> v;
        true -> {
            sequence proc[concurrency]
                ok: boolean <- cast(c.app, (:bees, 83, b.s1, b.s2, b.n, tn_now(c, v) * 65536 + b.m, b.who) impl ActorMessage {})
            produces pure v end
        }
    }
}
// ---- the stores' answers for accepted connections (121, 122, 126)
fn tn_answer(v: $NV$, tag: int64, k: int64, body: string) -> $NV$ {
    p: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_cid(v.q, tag, 1, 1);
    sequence
        _: atom <- case k == 21 of { true -> tn_say(concat("[tempus audit] shuffle_refused peer=- the store refused the frame a", tn_num(tag))); false -> :ok };
        _: boolean <- case p.k == 0 of { true -> true; false -> tn_ans(p.who, k, body) }
    produces pure tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_drop(v.q, p)) end
}
fn tn_sampled(v: $NV$, st: int64, ok: int64, body: string) -> $NV$ {
    p: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_first(v.q, 2, st);
    held: $P$ <- { k: 8, cid: p.cid, st: p.st, x: ok, who: p.who, s: body };
    case p.k == 0 of {
        true -> v;
        false -> case p.x == 1 of {
            true -> tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_swap(v.q, p, held));
            false -> {
                sequence
                    _: boolean <- tn_ans(p.who, case ok == 1 of { true -> 20; false -> 21 }, body)
                produces pure tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_drop(v.q, p)) end
            }
        }
    }
}
// Ruling NQ-12: the sentinel that answered a sample goes into the node's sentinel store at age 0 (an entry of it already
// there only becomes younger), after the sample's entries are in; the join goes on when that insert is in (k 9)
fn tn_keep_sentinel(v: $NV$, p: $P$, tag: int64) -> $NV$ {
    pd: { ok: boolean, d: $D$ } <- bees_tempus_frame@desc_of(p.s);
    d: $D$ <- pd.d;
    nx: $P$ <- { k: 9, cid: p.cid, st: p.st, x: p.x, who: p.who, s: "" };
    sequence
        _: boolean <- tn_to(v, 3, 44, d.id, p.s, tag)
    produces pure tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_swap(v.q, p, nx)) end
}
// an insert the node asked for is in its store (129): tag < 0 the join's (the dialed connection), else a sample's peer
fn tn_inserted(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, tag: int64) -> $NV$ {
    case tag < 0 of {
        true -> {
            p: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_cid(v.q, 0 - tag, 7, 7);
            p9: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_cid(v.q, 0 - tag, 9, 9);
            case p.k == 0 of {
                true -> case p9.k == 0 of { true -> v; false -> tn_join_ok(c, tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_drop(v.q, p9)), me, p9) };
                false -> case length_bytes(p.s) == 0 of {
                    true -> tn_join_ok(c, tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_drop(v.q, p)), me, p);
                    false -> tn_keep_sentinel(v, p, tag)
                }
            }
        };
        false -> {
            p: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_cid(v.q, tag, 2, 2);
            h: $P$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_cid(v.q, tag, 8, 8);
            fr: $P$ <- { k: 2, cid: p.cid, st: p.st, x: 0, who: p.who, s: "" };
            case p.k == 2 of {
                true -> tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_swap(v.q, p, fr));
                false -> case h.k == 8 of {
                    false -> v;
                    true -> {
                        sequence
                            _: boolean <- tn_ans(h.who, case h.x == 1 of { true -> 20; false -> 21 }, h.s)
                        produces pure tn_vq(v, bees_tempus_node@p_drop(v.q, h)) end
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

// a store wants draws (123): the converter is asked for one more than the shuffle length
fn tn_draws(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, st: int64, which: int64) -> $NV$ {
    sequence proc[concurrency]
        _: boolean <- cast(v.rc, (:bees, 1, "", "", (4 * st + which) * 1000 + tn_count(c, st) + 1) impl ActorMessage {})
    produces pure v end
}
// ---- start, the listener's events, the application's values
fn tn_arm(me: actor_ref, ms: uint64, st: int64) -> boolean {
    sequence proc[concurrency]
        t: timer_ref <- send_after(ms, me, (:bees, 1, "", "", 0, st, me) impl ActorMessage {})
    produces pure true end
}
fn tn_boot(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref) -> $NV$ {
    d: string <- bees_tempus_frame@desc_bytes(tn_desc(c, v));
    sequence proc[concurrency]
        z1: $AZ$ <- { typ: 1, id: c.id, d: d, own: c.typ == 1, cap: c.k1, count: c.c1, drv: c.driven, skew: c.skew, lit: c.draws };
        z2: $AZ$ <- { typ: 2, id: c.id, d: d, own: c.typ == 2, cap: c.k2, count: c.c2, drv: c.driven, skew: c.skew, lit: c.draws };
        z3: $AZ$ <- { typ: 3, id: c.id, d: d, own: c.typ == 3, cap: c.k3, count: c.c3, drv: c.driven, skew: c.skew, lit: c.draws };
        a1: actor_ref <- bees_tempus_node@adp_start(me, z1);
        a2: actor_ref <- bees_tempus_node@adp_start(me, z2);
        a3: actor_ref <- bees_tempus_node@adp_start(me, z3);
        rc: actor_ref <- spawn({ node: me, rnd: c.rnd, pend: "", got: "", bad: false }, dangerous_bees_tempus_draws@trc, stack_policy(0, :keep_last_message), state_policy(:keep_state_area));
        _: boolean <- case c.driven of { true -> true; false -> tn_arm(me, c.t1, 1) };
        _: boolean <- case c.driven of { true -> true; false -> tn_arm(me, c.t2, 2) };
        _: boolean <- case c.driven of { true -> true; false -> tn_arm(me, c.t3, 3) }
    produces pure { up: true, rc: rc, a1: a1, a2: a2, a3: a3, now: v.now, ck: v.ck, mtok: v.mtok, kid: v.kid, ppub: v.ppub, live: v.live, na: v.na, nd: v.nd, stop: v.stop, jst: v.jst, jd: v.jd, q: v.q } end
}
fn tn_store_line(st: int64, cap: int64, count: int64) -> atom {
    tn_say(concat(concat(concat("store ", tn_typ(st)), concat(": capacity ", tn_num(cap))), concat(", shuffle length ", tn_num(count))))
}
fn tn_up(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref) -> $NV$ {
    sequence
        _: atom <- tn_say(concat(concat(concat(tn_typ(c.typ), " node "), bees_tempus_node@peer8(c.id)), concat(" listening on ", c.addr)));
        _: atom <- tn_store_line(1, c.k1, c.c1);
        _: atom <- tn_store_line(2, c.k2, c.c2);
        _: atom <- tn_store_line(3, c.k3, c.c3)
    produces pure tn_join_start(c, v, me) end
}
fn tn_accepted(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, l: dangerous_actor_ref) -> $NV$ {
    // role 4 (ruling NQ-22): the system clock cannot be read and the node waits for it (clock_fail pause), so no token
    // can be judged; role 5: the node stopped after a step back above its limit (clock_back stop). Closed at once like role 3
    cl: int64 <- bees_tempus_node@clock_closes(v.ck);
    noclk: boolean <- cl != 0;
    full: boolean <- v.live >= c.max;
    over: boolean <- case noclk of { true -> true; false -> full };
    cfg: $CFG$ <- tn_cfg(c, v, me, tn_maxcount(c));
    role: int64 <- case noclk of { true -> cl; false -> case full of { true -> 3; false -> 2 } };
    sequence
        _: boolean <- tempus_conn(cfg, l, role, v.na + 1, "", "")
    produces pure tn_vc(v, case over of { true -> v.live; false -> v.live + 1 }, v.na + 1, v.nd) end
}
fn tn_token(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, token: string) -> $NV$ {
    v1: $NV$ <- tn_vk(v, v.now, token, v.kid, v.ppub, false);
    d: string <- bees_tempus_frame@desc_bytes(tn_desc(c, v1));
    sequence
        _: atom <- tn_say("own token replaced");
        _: boolean <- tn_to(v, 1, 47, "", d, 0);
        _: boolean <- tn_to(v, 2, 47, "", d, 0);
        _: boolean <- tn_to(v, 3, 47, "", d, 0)
    produces pure v1 end
}
fn tn_key(v: $NV$, kid: string, ppub: string) -> $NV$ {
    sequence
        _: atom <- tn_say(concat("producer key replaced, kid ", kid))
    produces pure tn_vk(v, v.now, v.mtok, kid, ppub, v.stop) end
}
// tag and who: 0 and the node itself from the node's own timer; a driver's on an externally driven node (tn_done). A
// node that is not driven reads neither, and an externally driven node arms no timer.
fn tn_timer(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, st: int64, tag: int64, who: actor_ref) -> $NV$ {
    p: $P$ <- { k: 3, cid: case c.driven of { true -> tag; false -> 0 }, st: st, x: 0, who: who, s: "" };
    ok: boolean <- st >= 1 and st <= 3;
    // no tick before the first reading of the system clock (v.ck 0 or 3): the node has not begun; none while the node
    // waits for its clock after a failed reading (v.ck 2; ruling NQ-22): its time stands still, so it admits and dials
    // nobody; none after it stopped for a step back above its limit (v.ck 4). It ticks with a good last reading (1),
    // while it holds its time (5) and while it goes on with its last reading after a failed one (6).
    ticks: boolean <- bees_tempus_node@clock_ticks(v.ck);
    case c.driven of {
        false -> {
            sequence
                _: boolean <- tn_arm(me, case st of { 1 -> c.t1; 2 -> c.t2; _: int64 -> c.t3 }, st)
            produces pure case ticks of { false -> v; true -> tn_tick(c, v, me, st, p) } end
        };
        // a driver's tick while the node does not tick (or for no store) has ended at once
        true -> case ticks and ok of {
            true -> tn_tick(c, v, me, st, p);
            false -> { sequence _: boolean <- tn_done(c, p.cid, p.who) produces pure v end }
        }
    }
}
// A reading of the clock (130, from the node's clock actor, or from the driver of an externally driven node; ruling NQ-11): n the seconds since 1970, or -1 when the
// operating system gave none. What it means is decided by bees_tempus_node@clock_turn (pure; it says what v.ck is and
// what each `say` is; ruling NQ-22 of 2026-11-20: clock_back and clock_fail are the application's choices). Here are the
// lines and the effects only. The first good reading starts the node: it listens (and joins when its link is up). A
// difference printed is a number of seconds, never a time of day.
fn tn_clock_line(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, say: int64, n: int64) -> atom {
    back: string <- concat(concat("the system clock went back by ", tn_num(v.now - n)), " s");
    case say of {
        1 -> tn_say("clock: the system clock is read");
        2 -> tn_say("clock: the system clock could not be read: the node has not started");
        3 -> tn_say("clock: the system clock could not be read: the node admits no connection and does not tick until it is read again");
        4 -> tn_say("clock: the system clock could not be read: the node goes on with its last reading");
        6 -> tn_say(concat(concat("clock: ", back), "; the node follows it"));
        7 -> tn_say(concat(concat("clock: ", back), "; the node holds its time until the system clock has reached it"));
        8 -> tn_say("clock: the system clock has reached the held time; the node follows it again");
        9 -> tn_say(concat("clock: ", tn_stop_why(c, v, n)));
        _: int64 -> :ok
    }
}
fn tn_stop_why(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, n: int64) -> string {
    concat(concat(concat("the system clock went back by ", tn_num(v.now - n)), concat(" s, more than clock_back_limit_s ", tn_num(c.blim))), ": the node has stopped; it admits no connection and does not tick until its application starts it again")
}
fn tn_clock_told(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, say: int64, n: int64) -> boolean {
    case say of {
        1 -> tempus_listen(me, c.listen, c.spec, c.ms);
        2 -> tn_app(c, me, 86, "the system clock could not be read: the node has not started");
        3 -> tn_app(c, me, 86, "the system clock could not be read: the node admits no connection and does not tick until it is read again");
        4 -> tn_app(c, me, 86, "the system clock could not be read: the node goes on with its last reading");
        9 -> tn_app(c, me, 87, tn_stop_why(c, v, n));
        _: int64 -> true
    }
}
fn tn_clock(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, n: int64) -> $NV$ {
    z: { back: int64, limit: int64, fail: int64 } <- { back: c.back, limit: c.blim, fail: c.fail };
    t: { now: int64, ck: int64, say: int64, again: boolean } <- bees_tempus_node@clock_turn(v.ck, v.now, n, z);
    sequence
        _: atom <- case t.again of { true -> tn_say("clock: the system clock is read again"); false -> :ok };
        _: atom <- tn_clock_line(c, v, me, t.say, n);
        _: boolean <- tn_clock_told(c, v, me, t.say, n)
    produces pure tn_clock_join(c, tn_vclk(v, t.now, t.ck), me, t.again) end
}
// a driver's reading with a tag (an externally driven node only) is acknowledged to the extension actor when it is taken
fn tn_clock_from(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, b: $NB$) -> $NV$ {
    v1: $NV$ <- tn_clock(c, v, me, b.n);
    case b.m != 0 and c.driven of {
        false -> v1;
        true -> {
            sequence proc[concurrency]
                ok: boolean <- cast(c.ext, (:bees, 132, "", "", b.m, 0, b.who) impl ActorMessage {})
            produces pure v1 end
        }
    }
}
// the join request that waited for the clock (tn_join) is made at once when the clock is read again
fn tn_clock_join(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, again: boolean) -> $NV$ {
    waits: boolean <- v.jst > 10;
    case again of {
        false -> v;
        true -> case waits of { false -> v; true -> tn_join(c, tn_vj(v, v.jst - 10, v.jd), me, v.jst - 10, 1) }
    }
}
fn tn_bees(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, b: $NB$) -> $NV$ {
    case b.op of {
        1 -> tn_timer(c, v, me, b.m, b.n, b.who);
        60 -> tn_dialed(c, v, me, b.op, b.s1, b.n, b.s2, b.m);
        61 -> tn_dialed(c, v, me, b.op, b.s1, b.n, "", 0);
        62 -> tn_dialed(c, v, me, b.op, b.s1, b.n, "", 0);
        67 -> tn_refused_peer(c, v, b);
        130 -> tn_clock_from(c, v, me, b);
        68 -> tn_rq_ext(c, v, b);
        63 -> { r: $RQ$ <- { body: b.s1, pd: b.s2, cid: b.n, m: b.m, who: b.who }; tn_request(c, v, me, r) };
        64 -> tn_vc(v, v.live - 1, v.na, v.nd);
        70 -> tn_token(c, v, b.s1);
        71 -> tn_key(v, b.s1, b.s2);
        // a join's retry timer: nothing is dialed after the node stopped for a step back (v.ck 4)
        72 -> case v.ck == 4 of { true -> v; false -> tn_join(c, v, me, b.n, 1) };
        120 -> tn_out(c, v, me, b.m, b.s1, b.s2);
        121 -> tn_answer(v, b.n, 20, b.s2);
        122 -> tn_answer(v, b.n, 21, "");
        124 -> tn_ended(c, v, me, b.m, b.n);
        125 -> { sequence _: atom <- tn_say(b.s1) produces pure v end };
        126 -> tn_sampled(v, b.m, b.n, b.s2);
        123 -> tn_draws(c, v, b.m, b.n);
        129 -> tn_inserted(c, v, me, b.n);
        128 -> { sequence _: boolean <- tn_to(v, b.m, 48 + b.n, "", b.s1, 0) produces pure v end };
        _: int64 -> v
    }
}
fn tn_handle(c: $NC$, v: $NV$, me: actor_ref, msg: $NM$) -> $NV$ {
    case msg of {
        (:accepted, l: dangerous_actor_ref, _i: string) -> tn_accepted(c, v, me, l);
        (:link_up, _info: string) -> tn_up(c, v, me);
        (:rx, _s: string) -> v;
        (:tx_credit, _n: int64) -> v;
        (:tx_failed, _w: atom) -> v;
        (:link_down, _w2: atom) -> { sequence _: atom <- tn_say("the listening link has gone down") produces pure v end };
        (:bees, op: int64, s1: string, s2: string, n: int64, m: int64, who: actor_ref) -> { b: $NB$ <- { op: op, s1: s1, s2: s2, n: n, m: m, who: who }; tn_bees(c, v, me, b) }
    }
}
fn tnode(msg: $NM$, st: $NS$) -> (:no_reply, $NS$) {
    sequence proc[concurrency]
        me: actor_ref <- self();
        v0: $NV$ <- case st.v.up of { true -> st.v; false -> tn_boot(st.c, st.v, me) };
        v: $NV$ <- tn_handle(st.c, v0, me, msg)
    produces pure (:no_reply, { c: st.c, v: v }) end
}
// T7: tempus_node_boot(idn, net, sz, drv) -> 0 to go on, 1 refused: the refusal is one line, "tempus: boot refused: WHY"
// (bees_tempus_node@boot_why: the bounds of section 8, the identity and its token, an externally driven node only on a
// loopback listen address). FIRST in main, as trust_boot. tempus_node_start refuses the same values (a line, the application told
// (:bees, 85, why, ...), the application itself returned, nothing started).
fn tempus_node_boot(idn: $NI$, net: $NN$, sz: $NZ$, drv: $NT$) -> int64 {
    why: string <- bees_tempus_node@boot_why(idn, net, sz, drv);
    case length_bytes(why) > 0 of {
        true -> { sequence _: atom <- tn_say(concat("tempus: boot refused: ", why)) produces pure 1 end };
        false -> 0
    }
}
fn tempus_node_start(app: actor_ref, idn: $NI$, net: $NN$, sz: $NZ$, drv: $NT$) -> actor_ref {
    why: string <- bees_tempus_node@boot_why(idn, net, sz, drv);
    case length_bytes(why) > 0 of {
        true -> {
            sequence proc[concurrency]
                _: atom <- tn_say(concat("tempus: boot refused: ", why));
                ok: boolean <- cast(app, (:bees, 85, why, "", 0, 0, app) impl ActorMessage {})
            produces pure app end
        };
        false -> tn_start(app, idn, net, sz, drv)
    }
}
fn tn_start(app: actor_ref, idn: $NI$, net: $NN$, sz: $NZ$, drv: $NT$) -> actor_ref {
    sequence proc[concurrency]
        e: dangerous_actor_ref <- spawn_dangerous(0, dangerous_bees_tempus_edge@ted, stack_policy(0, :keep_last_message), state_policy(:keep_state_area));
        r: dangerous_actor_ref <- spawn_dangerous(0, dangerous_bees_trust_edge@trnd, stack_policy(0, :keep_last_message), state_policy(:keep_state_area));
        sg: actor_ref <- tempus_signer(e, idn.seed);
        q: $PL$ <- bees_tempus_node@p_none();
        c: $NC$ <- { app: app, sig: sg, edge: e, rnd: r, wl: net.wl, sents: net.sents, listen: net.listen, spec: net.spec, mst: net.mst, id: idn.id, pub: idn.pub, addr: idn.addr, draws: drv.draws, typ: idn.typ, skew: net.skew, max: net.max, back: net.back, blim: net.blim, fail: net.fail, k1: sz.k1, c1: sz.c1, k2: sz.k2, c2: sz.c2, k3: sz.k3, c3: sz.c3, ms: net.ms, t1: sz.t1, t2: sz.t2, t3: sz.t3, j0: net.j0, j1: net.j1, driven: drv.driven, ext: drv.ext };
        v: $NV$ <- { up: false, rc: app, a1: app, a2: app, a3: app, now: 0, ck: 0, mtok: idn.token, kid: net.kid, ppub: net.ppub, live: 0, na: 0, nd: 0, stop: false, jst: 0, jd: net.j0, q: q };
        n: actor_ref <- spawn({ c: c, v: v }, tnode, stack_policy(0, :keep_last_message), state_policy(:keep_state_area));
        // the node listens when the first reading has come (tn_clock): from its clock actor, started here, or, when it
        // is externally driven, from its driver; nothing is started for a driven node, which waits
        _: boolean <- case drv.driven of {
            true -> cast(drv.ext, (:bees, 133, net.listen, "", 0, 0, n) impl ActorMessage {});
            false -> {
                sequence proc[concurrency]
                    k: actor_ref <- spawn({ node: n, edge: e, every: net.every }, dangerous_bees_tempus_draws@tck, stack_policy(0, :keep_last_message), state_policy(:keep_state_area));
                    ok: boolean <- cast(k, (:bees, 1, "", "", 0) impl ActorMessage {})
                produces pure ok end
            }
        }
    produces pure n end
}
